<title>USA: Pennsylvania Power wins antitrust appeal.</title>
<headline>Pennsylvania Power wins antitrust appeal.</headline>
<dateline>ALLENTOWN, Pa. 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pennsylvania Power &amp; Light Co, a subsidiary of PP&amp;L Resources Inc, said Friday that a three-judge federal appeals panel has upheld a lower court's dismissal of an antitrust suit brought against it by an independent power producer.</p>
<p>The producer, Schuylkill Energy Resources Inc, alleged that PP&amp;L violated antitrust laws by curtailing certain power purchases from it.</p>
<p>It was the second time, said PP&amp;L, that a federal court has ruled that Schuylkill is its supplier, not its competitor.</p>
</text>
